[10.96, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u25cf triage_cluster\u001b[0m\u001b[2m({})\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[11.062, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m 2 nodes, 1 healthy\r\n"]
[11.063, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m \u001b[31mCRITICAL\u001b[0m slurm-c1  \u001b[1mescalate_hardware\u001b[0m  Hardware fault: the node registered with less hardware than configured. Keep it out of service.\r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  Yes. One of the two nodes needs attention, and it's critical.\r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  ## slurm-c1: `escalate_hardware` (critical)\r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  **Summary:** The node registered with less hardware than it's configured for. Keep it out of service.\r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.119, "o", "  **Evidence (from triage):**\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  - state `IDLE+DRAIN+INVALID_REG`; 0 of 2 CPUs allocated; GRES `gpu:fake:3`, none in use\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  - reason `\"gres/gpu count reported lower than configured (3 < 4)\"`, set 8s ago by `slurm`\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  - **6 drain/down events** for this node in the event window. The chronic threshold is 3, so this is a\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  repeat offender.\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  - slurmd registered 3 of the 4 configured GPUs\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  **Next steps:**\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  1. Keep it drained. Don't resume it until the hardware is fixed.\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  2. Open a hardware ticket with the reason text and the node serial. On real GPUs, get `nvidia-smi -q`\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  output and the dmesg Xid lines first.\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  3. After the repair, run a burn-in job in the `burnin` partition before returning it to batch.\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  **Suggested commands (for you to run):**\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  ```\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  scontrol show node slurm-c1\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  ssh slurm-c1 'journalctl -u slurmd -n 50; dmesg | tail -50'\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  sbatch -p burnin -w slurm-c1 --gres=gpu:4 burnin.sh   # after repair\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  ```\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  It's already drained, so nothing needs doing in Slurm right now. I haven't changed anything.\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  \r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  The other node looks healthy to Slurm. This check only covers what Slurm can see, so it doesn't include\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  hardware sensors or GPU telemetry. I can pull `node_detail` on slurm-c1 if you want the earlier drain\r\n"]
[17.12, "o", "  events for the ticket.\r\n"]
[19.099, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.099, "o", "\u001b[1m3. Try to put it back\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.099, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.099, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[1myou \u203a\u001b[0m "]
