[36.17, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u25cf drain_node\u001b[0m\u001b[2m({\"node\": \"slurm-c2\", \"reason\": \"CHG-1043 BIOS update tonight\"})\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[36.237, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m \u001b[32mdone\u001b[0m  scontrol update nodename=slurm-c2 state=drain reason=\"triage: CHG-1043 BIOS update tonight\"\r\n"]
[37.338, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u25cf node_detail\u001b[0m\u001b[2m({\"node\": \"slurm-c2\"})\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[37.427, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m slurm-c2: IDLE+DRAIN  reason: triage: CHG-1043 BIOS update tonight (set by labadmin)\r\n"]
[37.427, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m 0 running job(s), 3 recent, 8 drain/down event(s)\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  **slurm-c2 is drained** (`done: true`). The server ran:\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  \r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  ```\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  scontrol update nodename=slurm-c2 state=drain reason=\"triage: CHG-1043 BIOS update tonight\"\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  ```\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  \r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  I checked the node afterwards:\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  - The state is now `IDLE+DRAIN`, with the reason set by `labadmin` at 23:03:24.\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  - No jobs are running on it, so it's already empty and you can start the BIOS update now without waiting.\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  \r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  **Heads-up:** slurm-c1 is still drained for the GPU fault. With both nodes out, **the cluster has no\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  schedulable nodes** until one comes back. New jobs will queue.\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  \r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  After the BIOS update, tell me to resume slurm-c2 and I'll do it. I'll run triage on it first to make sure\r\n"]
[42.397, "o", "  it registered cleanly.\r\n"]
